  </svg>
</section>

<!-- TIME DIFFERENCE MECHANICS -->
<section class="method-section" id="time-difference" aria-labelledby="time-diff-heading">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Time Difference Mechanics</p>
    <h2 id="time-diff-heading">Analyzing the 6-Hour Gap: CET vs EST</h2>
    <p>
      The standard offset between Central European Time (CET, UTC+1) and Eastern Standard Time (EST, UTC-5) is <strong>6 hours</strong>. Because CET is located in Central Europe at UTC+1, while EST sits on the North American East Coast at UTC-5, EST is 6 hours behind CET when both standard time definitions apply.
    </p>
    <p>
      When it is 12:00 PM (Noon) in Paris or Berlin, local time in New York or Miami is 6:00 AM on the same day. When it is 6:00 PM CET in Europe, it is 12:00 PM (Noon) EST in Eastern North America.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 700px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 600 180" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <rect width="600" height="180" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      <g transform="translate(120, 90)">
