      </g>
      <g transform="translate(300, 90)">
        <text x="0" y="8" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="28" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">→</text>
        <rect x="-45" y="-30" width="90" height="24" rx="12" fill="#1b536e" />
        <text x="0" y="-14" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="800" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">-6 HOURS</text>
      </g>
      <g transform="translate(480, 90)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="50" fill="#12455d" stroke="#8fd7ff" stroke-width="3" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="-20" y2="20" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-30" stroke="#8fd7ff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <text x="0" y="70" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="14" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">EST (UTC-5)</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>UTC Offsets Explained</h3>
      <p>CET operates at UTC+1, while EST operates at UTC-5. Calculating the offset separation: (+1) - (-5) = 6 hours difference.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Spring & Autumn Shift Dynamics</h3>
      <p>Because the US and EU change daylight saving clocks on different Sundays in March and October/November, the offset shifts to 5 or 7 hours during transition weeks.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Core Collaboration Window</h3>
      <p>With a 6-hour difference, the primary window for real-time collaboration spans 3:00 PM – 6:00 PM CET, matching 9:00 AM – 12:00 PM EST.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 24-HOUR CONVERSION TABLE -->
<section class="examples-section" id="conversion-chart" aria-labelledby="chart-heading">
  <div>
